# Utils and hooks (minimal)

## `app/utils`

- Put reusable helper functions here.
- Keep utilities small and mostly side-effect free.
- Use `*.server.js` for server-only utilities.
- Do not place business workflows here (use `app/core`).
- Document every exported function with `@param` / `@returns` (see [jsdoc-types.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/jsdoc-types.mdc)).

## `app/hooks`

- Put reusable React state/effect logic here.
- Hook files should be named `use-*.jsx`.
- Hook functions should start with `use`.
- If logic does not need React, move it to `app/utils`.
- Document hook params and return values with JSDoc; add `@typedef` for context/value shapes when reused.

## Shared boundaries

- Keep data-layer workflows in routes and `app/core`, not in generic hooks/utils.
- Use `#/*` imports and omit extensions.
